<title>USA: Continued high pressure in Brazil coffee belt--WSC.</title>
<headline>Continued high pressure in Brazil coffee belt--WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, high pressure aloft over Brazil's coffee belt will continue to dominate the area for the next seven days, Weather Services Corp said in an update Friday.</p>
<p>Fair skies were observed in the coffee belt this morning. Low temperatures were in the 50s F (low to middle teens C). Some cooler temperatures were reported in the higher elevations of Western Minas Gerais, according to WSC.</p>
<p>Mostly fair skies are expected for the coming week. Temperature levels should stay near to above normal. Low temperatures are expected to range in the 50s to low 60s F.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no damamging cold weather in sight,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
